# URL of the Keystone app (project management), used by "Ouvrir dans Keystone".
NEXT_PUBLIC_KEYSTONE_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Where Codex keeps its local database and uploaded files (default: ./.data).
# CODEX_DATA_DIR=.data

# ── Database (src/db/index.ts) ──
# Shared EPC2I PostgreSQL server: schema codex, role codex_app (setup in the Matrix repository, infra/postgres/).
# Unset or empty: embedded PGlite in $CODEX_DATA_DIR/pglite (development, Mac app). Run time only: `next build`
# never connects to it. Codex applies its migrations at start-up (journal: codex.__drizzle_migrations).
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://codex_app:change-me@localhost:5432/epc2i
# Size of the connection pool (default 10).
# CODEX_DB_POOL=10
# 1: fill an empty server database with the demo data (beta only). The PGlite database is always filled.
# CODEX_SEED_DEMO=1

# ── Integration API (docs/api.md) ──
# Bearer token of POST /api/import (migration tool). Unset: the import API is disabled (503).
# CODEX_IMPORT_TOKEN=change-me
# Maximum size of an imported file, in MB (default 100).
# CODEX_IMPORT_MAX_MB=100
# Bearer token of POST /api/integrations/vigie (Vigie decisions webhook). Unset: the webhook is disabled (503).
# VIGIE_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=change-me
# Vigie API; while unset, Vigie decisions can be simulated from Codex by a records manager.
# VIGIE_API_URL=http://localhost:3200/api
# URL of the Vigie app, used by "Ouvrir dans Vigie".
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VIGIE_URL=http://localhost:3200

# ── File storage (src/lib/storage.ts) ──
# local (default): files under $CODEX_DATA_DIR/files. sharepoint: a SharePoint library driven by Codex through
# Microsoft Graph (app-only); only the file, its name and its version go to SharePoint, all metadata stays in Codex.
# CODEX_STORAGE=local
# CODEX_SP_TENANT_ID=
# CODEX_SP_CLIENT_ID=
# CODEX_SP_CLIENT_SECRET=
# CODEX_SP_DRIVE_ID=

# ── Schema declaration to Matrix (src/lib/matrix.ts) ──
# At startup, right after the migrations, Codex sends its database schema to Matrix (POST /api/declarations,
# contract matrix.schema/1). Unset: nothing is sent. Credentials in the URL (https://user:pass@…) are sent as Basic.
# MATRIX_URL=https://matrix.example.org
# Token shared with Matrix, sent in the X-Matrix-Token header.
# MATRIX_TOKEN=change-me
# Optional: also write the declaration (codex.json) into this folder.
# MATRIX_DECLARATIONS_DIR=
